pmc:AlvarTvm0109Payan a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tiruvāymoḻi 1.9.11: the decad is said to yield reaching the lord's feet"@en, "Tiruvāymoḻi 1.9.11: Frucht der Dekade: Das Erreichen der Füße des Herrn"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AlvarIppattu ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AlvarTiruvadi ;
    skos:note "Tamil: niccalum viṇṇappam ceyya nīḷ kaḻal ceṉṉi porumē. Bharati: will abidingly secure his lotus feet to those who sing it to the lord with feeling. Satyamurthi Ayyangar: the lord's feet will for ever crown the heads of those who recite these songs."@en ;
    skos:note "The Tamil sets the condition of daily petition (niccalum viṇṇappam ceyya), Bharati renders it as singing with feeling."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Alvar ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AlvarTiruvaymoli ;
    dcterms:source "Nammāḻvār, Tiruvāymoḻi 1.9.11 (Tamil, Project Madurai ed.; trans. Srirama Bharati and Sowbhagya Lakshmi, Melkote 1987; trans. S. Satyamurthi Ayyangar, Bombay 1981)" .

pmc:AlvarTvm0110Payan a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tiruvāymoḻi 1.10.11: the decad is said to yield knowledge and clarity of mind"@en, "Tiruvāymoḻi 1.10.11: Frucht der Dekade: Wissen und Klarheit des Geistes"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AlvarIppattu ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AlvarKalvi ;
    skos:note "Tamil: taṇivilar kaṟparēl kalvi vāyumē. Bharati: those who learn it will attain pure knowledge. Satyamurthi Ayyangar: those that learn with zeal and thirst insatiable will with knowledge divine be filled."@en ;
    skos:note "The Tamil sets the condition of learning without abating (taṇivilar)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Alvar ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AlvarTiruvaymoli ;
