pmc:AlvarTvm0201Payan a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.1.11: the decad is said to yield reaching Vaikuṇṭha or heaven"@en, "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.1.11: Frucht der Dekade: Das Erreichen Vaikuṇṭhas oder des Himmels"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AlvarIppattu ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AlvarVaikuntam ;
    skos:note "Tamil: cōrār viṭār kaṇṭīr vaikuntam tiṇṇaṉavē. Satyamurthi Ayyangar: those that are regular in reciting these stanzas shall surely enjoy for ever heavenly bliss."@en ;
    skos:note "Read in the Tamil and in the 1981 translation only: the stanza stands on pages 22 and 23 of the 1987 translation, which the scanned copy lacks; the errata of that edition confirm that the decad is printed there."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Alvar ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AlvarTiruvaymoli ;
    dcterms:source "Nammāḻvār, Tiruvāymoḻi 2.1.11 (Tamil, Project Madurai ed.; trans. S. Satyamurthi Ayyangar, Bombay 1981)" .

pmc:AlvarTvm0202Payan a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.2.11: the decad is said to yield freedom from want and poverty"@en, "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.2.11: Frucht der Dekade: Freiheit von Mangel"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AlvarIppattu ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AlvarNalkuravuIlamai ;
    skos:note "Tamil: ēttavallavarkku illai ōr ūṉamē. Bharati: those who recite it with devotion shall have no want. Satyamurthi Ayyangar: for those who learn and laud these songs, drawbacks there will be none."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Alvar ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AlvarTiruvaymoli ;
    dcterms:source "Nammāḻvār, Tiruvāymoḻi 2.2.11 (Tamil, Project Madurai ed.; trans. Srirama Bharati and Sowbhagya Lakshmi, Melkote 1987; trans. S. Satyamurthi Ayyangar, Bombay 1981)" .

pmc:AlvarTvm0204Payan a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.4.11: the decad is said to yield service to the lord and his devotees"@en, "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.4.11: Frucht der Dekade: Dienst am Herrn und an seinen Verehrern"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AlvarIppattu ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AlvarAtimai ;
    skos:note "Tamil: aṭi kūṭṭalākum am tāmamē. Bharati: is a worthy garland on his feet. Satyamurthi Ayyangar: those that recite these songs will have the fortune to offer lovely flowers at his feet."@en ;
    skos:note "The two translations divide: Bharati reads the line as saying what the decad is, a garland at the feet, and states no fruit for the reciter; Satyamurthi reads it as the reciter's fortune of offering flowers at the feet, and his note turns it into perennial service in the company of the eternal ones. Entered on the reading that names a fruit, with the division recorded."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Alvar ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AlvarTiruvaymoli ;
    dcterms:source "Nammāḻvār, Tiruvāymoḻi 2.4.11 (Tamil, Project Madurai ed.; trans. Srirama Bharati and Sowbhagya Lakshmi, Melkote 1987; trans. S. Satyamurthi Ayyangar, Bombay 1981)" .

pmc:AlvarTvm0205Payan a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.5.11: the decad is said to yield reaching Vaikuṇṭha or heaven"@en, "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.5.11: Frucht der Dekade: Das Erreichen Vaikuṇṭhas oder des Himmels"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AlvarIppattu ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AlvarVaikuntam ;
    skos:note "Tamil: kūṟutal vallār uḷarēl kūṭuvar vaikuntamē. Bharati: secures Vaikuntha for those who can recite it. Satyamurthi Ayyangar: will the high heaven attain."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Alvar ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AlvarTiruvaymoli ;
    dcterms:source "Nammāḻvār, Tiruvāymoḻi 2.5.11 (Tamil, Project Madurai ed.; trans. Srirama Bharati and Sowbhagya Lakshmi, Melkote 1987; trans. S. Satyamurthi Ayyangar, Bombay 1981)" .

pmc:AlvarTvm0206Payan a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.6.11: the decad is said to yield becoming the lord's devotee"@en, "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.6.11: Frucht der Dekade: Zum Verehrer des Herrn werden"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AlvarIppattu ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AlvarTamar ;
    skos:note "Tamil: icaiyoṭum paṇṇil pāṭavallār avar kēcavaṉ tamarē. Bharati: those who sing it will be devotees of Kesava. Satyamurthi Ayyangar: those that sing tunefully these songs will join the rank and file of Kecava's devotees."@en ;
    skos:note "The Tamil sets the condition of singing with melody, in a paṇ."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Alvar ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AlvarTiruvaymoli ;
    dcterms:source "Nammāḻvār, Tiruvāymoḻi 2.6.11 (Tamil, Project Madurai ed.; trans. Srirama Bharati and Sowbhagya Lakshmi, Melkote 1987; trans. S. Satyamurthi Ayyangar, Bombay 1981)" .

pmc:AlvarTvm0207Payan a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.7.13: the decad is said to yield reaching the lord's feet"@en, "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.7.13: Frucht der Dekade: Das Erreichen der Füße des Herrn"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AlvarIppattu ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AlvarTiruvadi ;
    skos:note "Tamil: paṇṇil paṉṉiru nāmap pāṭṭu aṇṇal tāḷ aṇaivikkumē. Bharati: those who can sing it will attain the lord's feet. Satyamurthi Ayyangar: will unto the Sire's feet bind the chanters."@en ;
    skos:note "The decad of the twelve names has thirteen stanzas and its fruit stands in the thirteenth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Alvar ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AlvarTiruvaymoli ;
    dcterms:source "Nammāḻvār, Tiruvāymoḻi 2.7.13 (Tamil, Project Madurai ed.; trans. Srirama Bharati and Sowbhagya Lakshmi, Melkote 1987; trans. S. Satyamurthi Ayyangar, Bombay 1981)" .

pmc:AlvarTvm0208Payan a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.8.11: the decad is said to yield rule over earth or heaven and reaching Vaikuṇṭha or heaven"@en, "Tiruvāymoḻi 2.8.11: Frucht der Dekade: Herrschaft über Erde oder Himmel und Das Erreichen Vaikuṇṭhas oder des Himmels"@de ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:AlvarIppattu ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:AlvarAlutal, pmc:AlvarVaikuntam ;
    skos:note "Tamil: vallār viṇṭalaiyil vīṟṟiruntu āḷvar. Bharati: those who sing it will rule over heaven and earth. Satyamurthi Ayyangar: will in high heaven flourish and partake of bliss supreme."@en ;
